# WebUI icons and copy

## Icons

- Use **`lucide-react` only** for icons. Do not add other icon packs (Font Awesome, heroicons, custom SVG icon sets, emoji-as-icons for chrome, etc.).
- Import named icons from `lucide-react` and keep sizing/stroke consistent with nearby UI.
- Prefer existing lucide icons over one-off inline SVGs for UI chrome.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
import { ChevronLeft, Loader2 } from "lucide-react";

// ❌ BAD — new icon library
import { FaChevronLeft } from "react-icons/fa";
```

## Internationalization

- All **user-facing copy** must go through i18n (`react-i18next` / `useTranslation`).
- Add or update keys in `webui/src/i18n/locales/<locale>/common.json` (keep locales in sync; at minimum update `en` and `zh-CN` when changing copy).
- Prefer stable nested keys (`settings.models.platformModels`) over ad-hoc English strings in JSX.
- Avoid hardcoding labels, buttons, empty states, errors, tooltips, and aria labels in components.
- `defaultValue` in `t(key, { defaultValue })` is only a temporary fallback while keys land — still add the real locale entries in the same change when practical.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<button>Save</button>
<span>No configured providers</span>

// ✅ GOOD
const { t } = useTranslation();
<button>{t("settings.actions.save")}</button>
<span>{t("settings.byok.noConfiguredProviders")}</span>
```

Non-copy exceptions (OK without i18n): protocol identifiers, model IDs, provider API names, file paths, and other machine/config values shown as raw data.

## Enforcement (mechanical)

Hard-coded **CJK** (Han) literals in `webui/src` are blocked outside allowlisted paths (`i18n/locales`, `tests`, `i18n/config.ts` native labels, `lib/utils/format.ts` greeting tokens):

| Gate | How |
|------|-----|
| ESLint | `minibot-i18n/no-cjk-copy` in `webui/eslint.config.js` |
| Script | `cd webui && npm run lint:i18n` (`scripts/check-no-cjk-copy.mjs`) |
| Git pre-commit | `.githooks/pre-commit` — enable with `bash scripts/install-git-hooks.sh` |
| Cursor | `.cursor/hooks.json` → deny `git commit` when staged WebUI fails the same check |

`npm run lint` runs ESLint then the CJK script. English literals are still guided by this rule; CJK is the commit-time hard gate.
